          "mcqs": "Q1. Which option is most directly associated with “Greek heritage”?\nA. None of the above\nB. Greek heritage\nC. Medieval period\nD. Modern period\nAnswer: Greek heritage\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ2. Which option is most directly associated with “Medieval period”?\nA. Modern period\nB. None of the above\nC. Medieval period\nD. Greek heritage\nAnswer: Medieval period\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ3. Which option is most directly associated with “Modern period”?\nA. Modern period\nB. Greek heritage\nC. Medieval period\nD. None of the above\nAnswer: Modern period\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Greek heritage?\nA: Greek heritage is a focused concept within “Western psychology: Greek heritage, medieval period and modern period”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Greek heritage\nA: definition and scope of Greek heritage; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Medieval period?\nA: Medieval period is a focused concept within “Western psychology: Greek heritage, medieval period and modern period”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Medieval period\nA: definition and scope of Medieval period; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Modern period?\nA: Modern period is a focused concept within “Western psychology: Greek heritage, medieval period and modern period”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Modern period\nA: definition and scope of Modern period; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Organize Western intellectual history into Greek, medieval and modern periods. Focus on how ideas about mind, knowledge and human nature changed across these periods.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nFoundations of Psychology: The book introduces psychology as the scientific study of behavior and mental life, then traces major historical schools and viewpoints. It presents the goals of scientific psychology—description, explanation, prediction and control—and discusses structuralism, functionalism, Gestalt psychology, psychoanalysis and behaviorism alongside biological, learning, cognitive, sociocultural and humanistic viewpoints. It also distinguishes major fields such as clinical, counseling, developmental, experimental and physiological psychology.",
          "source_scope": "Authoritative UGC NET Psychology syllabus + Prompts for notes.docx + Psychology: A Self-Teaching Guide. Generated practice is PYQ-style; attached-book self-test items are source-based.",
          "bookmarks": false,
