          "explanation": "Ontology asks what is assumed to exist; epistemology asks how knowledge is possible or justified; methodology concerns how inquiry is conducted. Learn the distinction and their relationship within a paradigm.",
          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nOntology asks what is assumed to exist; epistemology asks how knowledge is possible or justified; methodology concerns how inquiry is conducted. Learn the distinction and their relationship within a paradigm.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nOntology • Epistemology • Methodology\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
