          "explanation": "Make a paradigm comparison chart. For each paradigm, learn its assumptions about reality/knowledge and its preferred approach to inquiry. The syllabus expects these six named paradigms.",
          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nMake a paradigm comparison chart. For each paradigm, learn its assumptions about reality/knowledge and its preferred approach to inquiry. The syllabus expects these six named paradigms.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nPositivism • Post-Positivism • Critical perspective • Social Constructionism • Existential Phenomenology • Co-operative Enquiry\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
