          "title": "Research Problems, Variables, Hypotheses and Sampling",
          "explanation": "Build the research sequence: problem → variables → operational definitions → hypothesis → sampling. Be able to distinguish conceptual variables from their operational definitions.",
          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nBuild the research sequence: problem → variables → operational definitions → hypothesis → sampling. Be able to distinguish conceptual variables from their operational definitions.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nResearch problems • Variables • Operational definitions • Hypothesis • Sampling\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
