              "title": "Cohort studies",
              "content_notes": "Cohort studies follow a defined group of people who share a characteristic or exposure and examine outcomes over time or across relevant conditions. The uploaded NET material lists cohort studies among experimental-design-related coverage, but provides limited detail in the supplied section; retain the basic design distinction without importing unsupported technical claims.\n\nKEY POINTS\n• A cohort is a defined group followed as a unit of observation.\n• The design is useful for studying change or outcomes associated with an exposure.\n• Temporal ordering can be important in cohort research.\n• The supplied NET section gives outline-level coverage here.\n\nDISTINCTION / CAUTION\nDo not automatically label every longitudinal study a cohort study; the defining feature is the cohort-based grouping of participants.",
