          "flashcards": "Q: What is Limbic system?\nA: Limbic system is a focused concept within “Biological basis of emotion: The Limbic system, Hormonal regulation of behavior”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Limbic system\nA: definition and scope of Limbic system; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Hormonal regulation of behavior?\nA: Hormonal regulation of behavior is a focused concept within “Biological basis of emotion: The Limbic system, Hormonal regulation of behavior”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Hormonal regulation of behavior\nA: definition and scope of Hormonal regulation of behavior; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Study limbic-system involvement and hormonal regulation as biological bases of emotional behaviour.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nBiology of Behavior: The biology chapter explains how the nervous and endocrine systems contribute to behavior. It covers neuron structure and communication, neural impulses, synaptic transmission and neurotransmitters, and distinguishes central and peripheral nervous-system functions. It also introduces major brain structures, the autonomic nervous system, endocrine glands and biological influences on behavior such as arousal, stress, sleep and reproduction.",
