              "id": 1,
              "title": "Motivation in perception",
              "content_notes": "Motivation can influence perceptual interpretation by shaping perceptual sets and readiness to notice or interpret stimuli in particular ways. The uploaded NET material explicitly includes the role of motivation in perception.\n\nKEY POINTS\n• Perception is not completely independent of current needs and goals.\n• Motivational states can contribute to perceptual set.\n• The effect is interpretive rather than a change in the physical stimulus itself.\n• Motivation interacts with prior experience and expectations.\n\nDISTINCTION / CAUTION\nMotivation can bias perception, but this does not mean that motivation literally changes the external stimulus.",
