          "flashcards": "Q: What is Assumptions of signal detection theory?\nA: framework separating sensitivity to signals from decision criterion under uncertainty\nQ: Key points for Assumptions of signal detection theory\nA: hit; miss; false alarm; correct rejection\nQ: What is Applications of signal detection theory?\nA: framework separating sensitivity to signals from decision criterion under uncertainty\nQ: Key points for Applications of signal detection theory\nA: hit; miss; false alarm; correct rejection",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Study detection as a decision process influenced by signal strength, noise and response criteria, and learn its applications.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nPerception: The perception chapter examines how sensory information becomes an organized psychological experience. It covers the distinction between the geographical and psychological worlds, Gestalt organization and figure-ground perception, perceptual learning, constancies and illusions, and binocular and monocular depth cues. It also discusses movement perception and the status of unusual perceptual claims such as psi powers within scientific psychology.",
