          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nMake a multi-part revision map covering subliminal perception, information processing, cultural influences, perceptual styles, pattern recognition and ecological approaches.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nSubliminal perception • Factors related to subliminal perception • Information processing approach to perception • Culture and perception • Perceptual styles • Pattern recognition • Ecological perspective on perception\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
          "status": "Not started",
          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Subliminal perception”?\nA. Information processing approach to perception\nB. Culture and perception\nC. Subliminal perception\nD. Factors related to subliminal perception\nAnswer: Subliminal perception\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.\n\nPYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 2\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Factors related to subliminal perception”?\nA. Factors related to subliminal perception\nB. Subliminal perception\nC. Information processing approach to perception\nD. Culture and perception\nAnswer: Factors related to subliminal perception\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
          "mcqs": "Q1. Which option is most directly associated with “Subliminal perception”?\nA. Factors related to subliminal perception\nB. Information processing approach to perception\nC. Culture and perception\nD. Subliminal perception\nAnswer: Subliminal perception\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ2. Which option is most directly associated with “Factors related to subliminal perception”?\nA. Culture and perception\nB. Factors related to subliminal perception\nC. Subliminal perception\nD. Information processing approach to perception\nAnswer: Factors related to subliminal perception\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ3. Which option is most directly associated with “Information processing approach to perception”?\nA. Subliminal perception\nB. Factors related to subliminal perception\nC. Culture and perception\nD. Information processing approach to perception\nAnswer: Information processing approach to perception\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Subliminal perception?\nA: Subliminal perception is a focused concept within “Subliminal perception and related factors, information processing approach to perception, culture and perception, perceptual styles, Pattern recognition, Ecological perspective on perception”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Subliminal perception\nA: definition and scope of Subliminal perception; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Factors related to subliminal perception?\nA: Factors related to subliminal perception is a focused concept within “Subliminal perception and related factors, information processing approach to perception, culture and perception, perceptual styles, Pattern recognition, Ecological perspective on perception”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Factors related to subliminal perception\nA: definition and scope of Factors related to subliminal perception; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Information processing approach to perception?\nA: Information processing approach to perception is a focused concept within “Subliminal perception and related factors, information processing approach to perception, culture and perception, perceptual styles, Pattern recognition, Ecological perspective on perception”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Information processing approach to perception\nA: definition and scope of Information processing approach to perception; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Culture and perception?\nA: Culture and perception is a focused concept within “Subliminal perception and related factors, information processing approach to perception, culture and perception, perceptual styles, Pattern recognition, Ecological perspective on perception”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Culture and perception\nA: definition and scope of Culture and perception; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Make a multi-part revision map covering subliminal perception, information processing, cultural influences, perceptual styles, pattern recognition and ecological approaches.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nPerception: The perception chapter examines how sensory information becomes an organized psychological experience. It covers the distinction between the geographical and psychological worlds, Gestalt organization and figure-ground perception, perceptual learning, constancies and illusions, and binocular and monocular depth cues. It also discusses movement perception and the status of unusual perceptual claims such as psi powers within scientific psychology.",
          "source_scope": "Authoritative UGC NET Psychology syllabus + Prompts for notes.docx + Psychology: A Self-Teaching Guide. Generated practice is PYQ-style; attached-book self-test items are source-based.",
