          "explanation": "Study how concepts are formed, the roles of rules/types/strategies, and the major forms of reasoning.",
          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nStudy how concepts are formed, the roles of rules/types/strategies, and the major forms of reasoning.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nRules of concept formation • Types of concepts • Strategies of concept formation • Role of concepts in thinking • Types of reasoning\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
