              "id": 1,
              "title": "Rules of concept formation",
              "content_notes": "Concept formation involves organizing experiences into categories that allow people to identify, classify and reason about objects or events. The uploaded sources emphasize concepts as tools for organizing everyday experience and thinking.\n\nKEY POINTS\n• Concepts group related instances.\n• Categorization reduces the complexity of experience.\n• Rules or defining features can guide category membership.\n• Concepts support reasoning and problem solving.\n\nDISTINCTION / CAUTION\nA concept is a mental category; a rule is a criterion or strategy used to form or apply that category.",
