              "title": "Strategies of concept formation",
              "content_notes": "Concept formation can use strategies that compare examples, identify common features and test possible rules. The uploaded material places strategies of concept formation within the broader study of thinking and reasoning.\n\nKEY POINTS\n• People compare instances when forming categories.\n• Relevant similarities and differences help refine a concept.\n• Hypotheses about category membership can be tested against examples.\n• Experience can improve categorization efficiency.\n\nDISTINCTION / CAUTION\nA concept-formation strategy is a cognitive procedure; it is not itself the final concept.",
