              "content_notes": "Decision making involves selecting among alternatives. The uploaded material distinguishes decision making from problem solving and treats types and models of decision making as a core cognitive topic.\n\nKEY POINTS\n• Decision making requires alternatives and a choice.\n• Choices may be made under different levels of information and uncertainty.\n• Cognitive biases can affect decisions.\n• Decision-making models describe how alternatives are evaluated.\n\nDISTINCTION / CAUTION\nDecision making is not identical to problem solving: problem solving seeks a route to a goal, whereas decision making selects among alternatives.",
