          "title": "Determinants of Personality",
          "explanation": "Compare biological and sociocultural influences on personality and consider their interaction.",
          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nCompare biological and sociocultural influences on personality and consider their interaction.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nBiological determinants • Socio-cultural determinants\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
          "status": "Not started",
          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Biological determinants”?\nA. Biological determinants\nB. Socio-cultural determinants\nC. None of the above\nD. None of the above\nAnswer: Biological determinants\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.\n\nPYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 2\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Socio-cultural determinants”?\nA. Biological determinants\nB. None of the above\nC. None of the above\nD. Socio-cultural determinants\nAnswer: Socio-cultural determinants\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
          "mcqs": "Q1. Which option is most directly associated with “Biological determinants”?\nA. None of the above\nB. Biological determinants\nC. Socio-cultural determinants\nD. None of the above\nAnswer: Biological determinants\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ2. Which option is most directly associated with “Socio-cultural determinants”?\nA. Socio-cultural determinants\nB. Biological determinants\nC. None of the above\nD. None of the above\nAnswer: Socio-cultural determinants\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Biological determinants?\nA: Biological determinants is a focused concept within “Determinants of personality: Biological and socio-cultural”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Biological determinants\nA: definition and scope of Biological determinants; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Socio-cultural determinants?\nA: Socio-cultural determinants is a focused concept within “Determinants of personality: Biological and socio-cultural”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Socio-cultural determinants\nA: definition and scope of Socio-cultural determinants; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Compare biological and sociocultural influences on personality and consider their interaction.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nPersonality: The personality chapter defines personality as a distinctive pattern of traits and processes and compares type-trait, psychodynamic, neo-Freudian, learning and humanistic approaches. It covers Freud's id, ego and superego, Jung's archetypes and collective unconscious, Adlerian ideas, learning-based personality formation and Maslow's humanistic perspective. It also introduces personality assessment, including objective and projective approaches such as the Rorschach and MMPI.",
          "source_scope": "Authoritative UGC NET Psychology syllabus + Prompts for notes.docx + Psychology: A Self-Teaching Guide. Generated practice is PYQ-style; attached-book self-test items are source-based.",
          "bookmarks": false,
