              "id": 1,
              "title": "Nature of social psychology",
              "content_notes": "Social psychology studies how people think about, influence and relate to other people. The uploaded NET material emphasizes the social context of behavior, while Kaplan organizes the field around social perception, attitudes, group processes and social influence.\n\nKEY POINTS\n• Social context is central to explanation.\n• The field examines cognition, affect and behavior in social situations.\n• Individuals and groups are both relevant levels of analysis.\n• Social psychology connects individual processes with interpersonal and group contexts.\n\nDISTINCTION / CAUTION\nSocial psychology is not simply the study of groups; many social-psychological processes occur at the individual level in social contexts.",
