          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Counselling process”?\nA. None of the above\nB. Counselling process\nC. Counselling skills\nD. Counselling techniques\nAnswer: Counselling process\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.\n\nPYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 2\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Counselling skills”?\nA. Counselling techniques\nB. None of the above\nC. Counselling skills\nD. Counselling process\nAnswer: Counselling skills\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
          "mcqs": "Q1. Which option is most directly associated with “Counselling process”?\nA. Counselling techniques\nB. None of the above\nC. Counselling process\nD. Counselling skills\nAnswer: Counselling process\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ2. Which option is most directly associated with “Counselling skills”?\nA. Counselling process\nB. Counselling techniques\nC. None of the above\nD. Counselling skills\nAnswer: Counselling skills\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ3. Which option is most directly associated with “Counselling techniques”?\nA. Counselling techniques\nB. Counselling process\nC. Counselling skills\nD. None of the above\nAnswer: Counselling techniques\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Counselling process?\nA: structured helping process involving rapport, assessment, goals, intervention and follow-up\nQ: Key points for Counselling process\nA: rapport; assessment; goals; intervention\nQ: What is Counselling skills?\nA: active listening, empathy, reflection, questioning, summarizing and appropriate silence\nQ: Key points for Counselling skills\nA: attending; empathy; reflection; open questions\nQ: What is Counselling techniques?\nA: Counselling techniques is a focused concept within “Counselling: Process, skills, and techniques”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Counselling techniques\nA: definition and scope of Counselling techniques; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Study counselling as a helping process, emphasizing process stages, core skills and techniques.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nTherapy: The therapy chapter distinguishes psychologically based and biologically based approaches to helping people with mental and emotional problems. It covers psychoanalysis and free association, client-centered therapy and unconditional positive regard, behavior therapy and operant conditioning, rational-emotive behavior therapy, cognitive-behavior therapy, group approaches and major classes of psychiatric medication. Different therapies are presented as being based on different explanations of psychological difficulty.",
